Optional compatibility work, not a requirement for the shared platform.
Markus Frank's v4 patch retains his authorship and sign-off. It was adapted
to the current VGA code and checked with the shared D-Bus configuration.
Apply after the shared base (and the WebRTC series if using QSM).

Configuration tests cover a shared GL display with blobs and rejection of
VirGL features on non-GL VGA. Full cfg2cmd checks pass. Vulkan/OpenGL 4.6
inside a guest was not runtime-qualified in this work. This does not claim
that the underlying QEMU/VirGL Venus patches have been merged.

Dmitry R (1):
  test: exercise shared D-Bus display with optional VirGL blobs

Markus Frank (1):
  fix #6277: virtio-vga-gl: add OpenGL 4.6 and Vulkan (Venus) support

